Gateway bundles third-party code:

  third_party/certainly            MIT, github.com/minorbug/certainly
                                   minorbug's TLS 1.3 client for Mac OS 9.
                                   Vendored and patched; see PATCHES.md for
                                   every change and why it was needed.

  third_party/certainly/bearssl    MIT, bearssl.org
                                   Thomas Pornin's BearSSL. The reason a TLS
                                   1.3 client on a 1999 machine is possible at
                                   all: self-contained, constant-time, and
                                   correct on a big-endian PowerPC and a
                                   little-endian x86 alike, unmodified.

  third_party/InterfacesAndLibraries
                                   Apple Universal Interfaces & Libraries,
                                   redistributed under Apple's SDK licence.
                                   Not covered by the MIT grant above.

Gateway also stands on work it does not bundle:

  Retro68                          github.com/autc04/Retro68
                                   Wolfgang Thaller's cross toolchain and the
                                   Multiversal Interfaces. Without it there is
                                   no way to build a modern C++ Classic
                                   application at all.

  WaybackProxy                     github.com/richardg867/WaybackProxy
                                   richardg867's Internet Archive proxy, the
                                   prior art for Module 3. Its settings URL is
                                   the interface Gateway's Wayback proxy
                                   copies, so existing bookmarks keep working.
                                   That project is GPL-3 and Gateway is MIT,
                                   so no code was taken: Module 3 is an
                                   independent implementation written from the
                                   archive's public URL scheme and observable
                                   behaviour. The design is its own; the idea
                                   is not.

  email-oauth2-proxy               github.com/simonrob/email-oauth2-proxy
                                   simonrob's OAuth2 proxy: where the
                                   out-of-band consent flow that produces
                                   Gateway's refresh token happens, and whose
                                   config format
                                   tools/extract-refresh-token.py reads.

  FrogFind                         frogfind.com
                                   Action Retro's search engine and page
                                   simplifier for vintage machines, which is
                                   what a good deal of the testing was pointed
                                   at.
